# S10.2D Control hash-binding regression diagnosis

Date: 2026-09-05

## Symptom

The first complete Control test run reported three SHA-256 mismatches for the
shared S8 health executable, S8 runtime unit and S8 health unit. The changed
files were intentional S10.2D Community bindings, but the historical S8
manifest still referenced their prior deployable revisions.

## Cause

The repository treats current deployable Control files as hash-bound material
from every dependent manifest. Adding Community arguments changed those files
without simultaneously advancing the S8 compatibility bindings.

## Resolution

The S8 manifest now binds the exact new revisions. The S10.1 manifest likewise
binds the evolved backup, health, WMS and shared S9-health files. No runtime or
server state was changed. Targeted S10.1/S10.2B/S10.2D tests pass after the
update; the complete suite is rerun before commit.

## Prevention

Every future shared unit, health executable or backup-script change must update
all manifests that intentionally verify the current deployable file, not only
the newest phase manifest.
